2026-09-28: original GCC stall captured; cause still OPEN.

The unchanged stress_04 again reaches its original 45-second limit. At 25 s,
40 s and before shutdown sync, writeback workers flush-259:5 / flush-259:8
remain in blk_mq_get_tag -> __blk_mq_alloc_requests -> blk_mq_submit_bio ->
submit_bh_wbc -> block_write_full_folio -> blkdev_writepages -> wb_workfn.
fio/io_uring workers wait for folios in filemap_get_pages / filemap_read.
Available memory is about 1.77 GiB; dirty bytes fall from about 88 MiB to
66 MiB while writeback remains 2484 KiB. This is blocked request/writeback
progress, not evidence that the machine ran out of RAM.

The outer script exits zero after the inner TIMEOUT, but the existing parser
correctly records FAIL. Shutdown sync does not complete; outer boot TIMEOUT
105 s. No timeout or source is changed. This capture is GCC reference evidence,
not an EvoCC miscompilation diagnosis. Leaders with wchan=0 are not sufficient
evidence to label them zombies; thread states and device/queue mapping were
not captured by that observer revision.

The observer now also collects cmdline/status, each kublk thread's wait stack,
and each ublk device's inflight/stat and bounded debugfs queue state. Two
three-pair runs with that added observation all pass: 6 GCC + 6 EvoCC original
invocations and shutdowns. They do not erase the captured failure or identify
a repair. Per-file reads are capped at 4096 bytes, kmsg at 256 records, thread
enumeration at 64 per leader; these are deliberately partial observations.
The optional UBLK_DIAGNOSTIC_PROBE build executes ublk-kill-cancel instead of
the original runner, while retaining the shared nonce/timeout/shutdown path.
It is separately labeled diagnostic and is never original-program credit.

